en:
&lt;The tauren carefully looks over your handiwork, brows furrowed.&gt;

You've learned some things, I see.

Very well. You have succeeded.

ua:
&lt;Таурен уважно оглядає твою роботу, насупивши брови.&gt;

Я бачу, ти дечого навчи$p(вся:лася).

Що ж. Ти впора$p(вся:лася).

en:
&lt;Raegar wipes his forehead with the back of his hand.&gt;

Oh, no. This is going to be harder than I thought. These things don't have serial numbers or anything, do they?

Never a gnome around when you need one...

The Grimtotem...

&lt;Mull scowls.&gt;

I'd hoped to see the end of my days before &lt;race&gt; attacked other &lt;race&gt; senselessly on the very plains of Mulgore.  But be proud, &lt;name&gt;.  You have done a great thing for the land, and for our people.

Thank you for making the trip back down to my humble lair.

&lt;A deep chuckle rumbles out from Widow Arak'nai.&gt;

We have got grand plans in store for you. Certainly, certainly.

You are very courageous to bring us this information. I was beginning to wonder why the blue dragonflight had so boldly initiated an attack upon the temple itself. Now we know that they are using enormous amounts of the very magic they view as such a threat to Azeroth.

&lt;The queen shakes her head in seeming resignation.&gt;

Hypocritical, but so be it. If Malygos will not come to his senses, we have no choice but to take action in response to their assault.

ua:
Дуже відважно з твого боку принести нам ці відомості. Я вже почала дивуватися, чому синій драконячий переліт так сміливо напав на сам храм. Тепер ми знаємо, що вони використовують величезні обсяги тієї самої магії, яку вважають такою загрозою для Азероту.

&lt;Королева похитує головою, ніби змирившись.&gt;

Лицемірство, але нехай так. Якщо Маліґос не прийде до тями, нам не лишається нічого, окрім як відповісти на їхній напад.

en:
&lt;Brewston leans in close to you and speaks just above a whisper.&gt;

I'm glad I found you. I need all the allies I can get.

You're very lucky they left you alive.

&lt;Thaedris stirs from his thoughts as you approach.&gt;

These will be sufficient, &lt;race&gt;.

 Cliffthorn is a deadly poison, and will be perfect for my needs.

ua:
&lt;Таедріс виринає зі своїх думок, коли ти наближаєшся.&gt;

Цього буде достатньо, {race}.

 Скелешип — смертельна отрута, саме те, що мені потрібно.

en:
&lt;Zinnia carefully examines the heirloom&gt;

Did a duck gnaw on this? This is going to take some elbow grease to polish out!

Thank you for your help, &lt;name&gt;.

ua:
&lt;Зінія уважно оглядає реліквію&gt;

Це що, качка гризла? Доведеться добряче попотіти, щоб це відполірувати!

Дякую за допомогу, &lt;name&gt;.

en:
&lt;Faerin breathes deeply.&gt; 

Even from here... I can almost feel it. Beledar's strength returning. You've helped push back the darkness. 

Thank you.

Did you get stung by any bees? Did you feel the burn? Maybe you're allergic.

&lt;Faerin chuckles.&gt;

What? That wasn't a funny enough joke? Then you do better!

What have you brought today, Archmage?

&lt;Edirah examines the ancient tome.&gt;

This book... it changes everything!

ua:
Що ти $p(приніс:принесла) сьогодні, Архімаже?

&lt;Едіра оглядає прадавній фоліант.&gt;

Ця книга... вона все змінює!

en:
By the Light! I thought I lost it forever!

This used to belong to my great grandfather.

&lt;Myra clutches the necklace close to her heart for a moment as a tear runs down her cheek. After a moment, she looks around, shaking her head.&gt;

Nothing here can remotely repay this. It's not much, but I can show you how to get the most out of mining monelite seams.

&lt;Myra spends the next several minutes explaining several techniques to increase the amount of monelite mined from a seam.&gt;

Are they alive? Good. Next time they forget to check in, they won't be.

&lt;Ve'nari skims through the reports.&gt;

It looks like there was minimal damage, if any at all, to most of the facility. The Shadowguard saboteurs were focused on rerouting our energy reserves to the outer conduits. They have ignored the environmental and secondary systems.

Well now, this is a good variety of equipment you've brought me. Let's see what we have here...

&lt;Diane studies the armor pieces very carefully for a while.&gt;

Look here, &lt;name&gt;. See how they've strengthened the leather by over-stitching the seams...

ua:
Ну що ж, непогане розмаїття спорядження ти мені $p(приніс:принесла). Подивімося, що тут є...

&lt;Діана якийсь час дуже уважно вивчає частини обладунку.&gt;

Поглянь сюди, {name}. Бачиш, як вони зміцнили шкіру подвійним прошиванням швів...

en:
&lt;Marley's eyes sparkle as you rush toward him with the ale. He grasps the mug in both of his shaking hands and upends it, white foam spilling out over his blood-caked beard.&gt;

Ah... that's the stuff. Ol' Barkerstout... Thank you, friend.

That'll make this... a little easier.

&lt;Coughing one final time, he slumps over the shattered control console, the half-empty mug crashing to the ground and spilling its contents into the sand. His eyes glaze over.&gt;

&lt;Marley Twinbraid is dead.&gt;

The foul weather offers us some cover. Every thick cloud and raindrop is an ally.

&lt;Shandris Feathermoon smirks.&gt;

In that sense, we actually outnumber the Horde. They don't stand a chance.

I did not expect... this. 

&lt;Lor'themar glances at Turalyon.&gt;

Perhaps we overstepped our bounds.

These are good pieces. Look here...

&lt;Celea begins to explain the armor's construction to you.&gt;

...and with that, I trust you can create something of equal quality.

ua:
Гарні деталі. Поглянь сюди...

&lt;Селея починає пояснювати тобі будову обладунку.&gt;

...і з цим, я певна, ти зможеш створити щось такої ж якості.

en:
Teamwork makes the dream work, or so they say. It would appear that the rhyme carries truth to it. Hmmm.

&lt;Eternus pauses for a moment in thought.&gt;

I wonder what other rhymes carry such power. That bears some future experimentation.

&lt;Diane examines the chest piece thoroughly.&gt;

This has some very interesting design. I think we can easily copy what they've achieved with this piece.

Here, try this pattern out.

ua:
&lt;Діана ретельно оглядає нагрудник.&gt;

Дуже цікавий задум. Гадаю, ми легко зможемо повторити те, чого тут досягнуто.

Ось, спробуй цю викройку.

en:
&lt;Alby clears his throat.&gt;

It is good to see the young lord safe.

...Thanks.

Oh SWEET justice! Killin' those kobolds won't make me walk like a normal person and it sure won't get me a job, but damn does it feel good.

&lt;Jimb reaches into a crusty old sack.&gt;

Here, I think I got somethin' for you from my kobold huntin' days. Maybe you can put it to good use.

One day, this island will belong to the Alliance. I can only hope that it will be free of saurok before then.

&lt;Modera sneers.&gt;

At least they attack the Horde, too.

You continue to amaze me!  Tell you what... why don't you come back tomorrow and we'll let the rope cool off for now?

&lt;Khatie laughs.&gt;

Thank you so much, &lt;name&gt;!

&lt;The fish gulps down saltwater to regain its breath and then turns to look at you with intelligent eyes.&gt;

I live, thanks to you. The shade of these rocks suits me nicely for the work to be done. 

Allow me to repay your selfless gesture.

&lt;Talanji listens to your tale of Xal'atath and N'Zoth.&gt;

Zandalar is still reeling from de Old God's infestation in Uldir. If another rises...

Dis is troubling news indeed. Only together can we turn back dis tide.

Oh. I don't like this herb at all. I'm fascinated, but I don't like it.

&lt;Kuhuine peers into the center of the plant.&gt;

Look at the size of these seeds, &lt;name&gt;. We can use these. Make sure you harvest them carefully next time.

&lt;Lard takes the huge haunch of meat from you and stuffs it in his face.&gt;

Dis hit da spot! Tanks little one.

Lard make you special picnic basket for help Lard.

&lt;Chu'a'lor nods his heads at you in satisfaction at your accomplishment.&gt;

You have a quick mind, &lt;name&gt;.  It took us much longer to successfully make use of the relic.

Now that you know how, you can do so as much as you care to.  Just remember that they require an apexis shard to power them.

Maddening! I am no closer to a breakthrough on this matter. Such a failure is unacceptable!

&lt;Vridiel breathes deeply and composes himself.&gt;

Thank you, &lt;name&gt;. I must not let this setback deter me from further attempts. Please, take this. You will no doubt find a use for it.

Your power has grown, my faithful knight.

&lt;Highlord Darion Mograine peers at you.&gt;

Vengeance is at hand, brother. Koltira aids the Horde upon the gunship, Orgrim's Hammer, while Thassarian assists the Alliance aboard the Skybreaker. The Ebon Blade will soon wash over Icecrown and leave the armies of the Lich King in ruin.

&lt;As the king examines the compass, his expression turns from recognition to sorrow.&gt;

When I went through my father's things and didn't find this compass, I assumed it was with him on the Broken Shore when Gul'dan...

&lt;The king's voice breaks.&gt;

ua:
&lt;Поки король роздивляється компас, впізнавання на його обличчі змінюється смутком.&gt;

Коли я розбирав речі батька і не знайшов цього компаса, я вирішив, що він був при ньому на Зламаному Березі, коли Гул'дан...

&lt;Голос короля зривається.&gt;

en:
&lt;Garrosh crumples up the map and throws it into the fire.&gt;

What's the use? They've been attacking us for weeks. This is nothing new.

Don't you understand? We're done for... Greatmother Geyah is dying.

Ho ho, what's this?

&lt;Uncle Gao jiggles his fat brew belly at the sight of the family's recipes.&gt;

Ooh, I knew I was adding too much corn!

Good! This is the perfect size for some of the smaller, more delicate work, the kind that would break needles constantly.

Are you ready for your lesson?

&lt;Camilla spends the next several minutes showing you how to dislocate and quickly flay bones that were previously too time consuming to bother trying to collect.&gt;

You say the demons were all worshipping the tree?

&lt;The mayor sighs.&gt;

It is as I feared, then.

&lt;The Professor dips his finger into the fluid and tastes it.&gt;

Oh! I know what this is. The herbalists were talking about this. It's called fjarnsk.

You know, stranglekelp often contains pockets of fluid not unlike this. Let's see if we can carry an old milling technique forward...

Yes, this will work.

&lt;Banthok expertly manipulates the key fragments.&gt;

Here it is, &lt;class&gt;. With this key, my father will be freed of the Anub'ar prison.

You're certain nobody saw you?  Good.

&lt;Netherwane listens to your recount of the information you saw.&gt;

Hmph... fairly harmless stuff.  Either the Horde are foolish enough to NOT be planning something against us... or they're hiding their information better than I expected.  Either way, well done, soldier.

We think we seen you before. You visit Mistwhisper village sometime already?

Soo-say said you good. Soo-say smart, so we trust you too.

&lt;Mistcaller Soo-gan offers an awkwardly large smile.&gt;

ua:
Ми думати, ми тебе бачити раніше. Ти вже приходити до села Шепіт Туману?

Су-сей казати, ти добрий. Су-сей розумний, тому ми теж тобі вірити.

&lt;Покликач Туману Су-ґан незграбно широко всміхається.&gt;

en:
Yes, this is it.

&lt;Jace turns the rune over in his hands, studying the intricate markings.&gt;

Excellent work, &lt;name&gt;. I'll make sure Nalthanis is made aware of your contribution.

&lt;Fareeya examines the crystal fragment.&gt;

This is old... very old. It is a piece of an elaborate key, the sort my people use to secure our most prized and sacred places.

I wonder...

&lt;Osme looks at the herb.&gt;

&lt;He is silent for a moment.&gt;

NOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO!!!!!!

&lt;Kuhuine listens to your story about the aethril.&gt;

What you're saying rings true, &lt;name&gt;. I have heard tales of herbalists that could coax flowers into quickly reproducing, but I was never able to master the technique myself.

Well done, herbalist. I feel great pride.

&lt;Kaide nods at you.&gt;

Well done. We have bought ourselves a little time. The blood elves will grow curious about what happened to their friend. Hopefully, by that time, we will have a better understanding of their intentions.

When the time is right, I will inform Rogak of our progress.

&lt;Mountaineer Kilian listens as you relate what the captive prospectors told you.&gt;

They mentioned Loken and a war against stone giants? You're certain?

So Raegar's instincts were right. We have to find a way to get in there and learn more about their plans.

You got our ammo and I got our air support.

&lt;Flynn gestures to Taelia and Galeheart with a grin.&gt;

You see where I'm going with this.

&lt;Mor'ghor reads the letter and laughs.&gt;

A death knight? You couldn't shine the boots of a death knight, maggot.

&lt;Mor'ghor looks you over.&gt;

But yes... You might be able to work your way up to peon. At the worst, I'll toss you into the pit and leave you to die...

Ah, you found it! Excellent.

&lt;Lucille produces a long sewing needle from the kit&gt;

...You look confused. Let me explain.

Ah, dis be it, mon.

&lt;The lens glows brightly in Buunu's hands, casting unearthly rays of light across the shadowy cave mouth.&gt;

We be ready to bring dem spirits out de shadows now.

&lt;Camilla takes a moment to look over the hides.&gt;

Acceptable work. We'll lose some material trimming, but there should be enough to encompass our esteemed and honorable benefactor.

Also, I think I see an error that, if corrected, could help when you're harvesting from anything with scales. Show me what you did.

&lt;Camilla hands you a knife and watches your movements as you explain. She occasionally stops you to adjust the position of your hands and states that it'll help next time.&gt;

And just what is this?

&lt;Moira takes the report and the color drains from her face as she reads.&gt;

This is impossible!

Velonara asked you to deliver this to me personally?

&lt;Moorgoth's eyes sparkle as he grins from ear to ear.&gt;

She DOES care! She DOES care!

&lt;Moorgoth settles down and clears his throat.&gt;

That was kind of her. Say, it is a nice hood. I bet I could mass-produce this and offer it to my fellow dark ranger aficionados.

Would you like to browse my wares?

ua:
Велонара попросила тебе передати це мені особисто?

&lt;Очі Мургота спалахують, і він розпливається в усмішці від вуха до вуха.&gt;

Вона таки дбає про мене! Таки дбає!

&lt;Мургот заспокоюється і прочищає горло.&gt;

Це було дуже мило з її боку. До речі, гарний каптур. Б'юся об заклад, я міг би налагодити їхнє масове виробництво й пропонувати моїм друзям-шанувальникам темних слідопитів.

Хочеш поглянути на мій товар?

en:
I once studied here. And now...

&lt;Zelling clears his throat.&gt;

We have a job to do.

&lt;Harry takes the crystal from you and gently pets it.&gt;

Oh my precious! Did the big, mean whale hurt you? It'll be ok. I'll never let you out of my sight again!

&lt;Harry looks up at you.&gt;

So, where were we?

&lt;Flem weighs the gems in his hands and nods in approval.&gt;

Yes, these will do.  Now to perform the analysis...

&lt;The goblin clacks the gems together for a while, then looks up at you.&gt;

Oh, you're still here?  You don't think I'm a fraud or something, do you?

ua:
&lt;Флем зважує самоцвіти в руках і схвально киває.&gt;

Так, ці підійдуть. А тепер проведемо аналіз...

&lt;Ґоблін якийсь час постукує самоцвітами один об одного, а потім дивиться на тебе.&gt;

О, ти ще тут? Ти ж не думаєш, що я якийсь шахрай, чи не так?

en:
&lt;Lathorius takes the halberd from you.&gt;

Is this what I think it is?

&lt;Lathorius grins.&gt;

Smashing! Outstanding! Another of Nesingwary's lackeys brought to justice!

You discovered and put an end to the doctor's machinations.

&lt;The banshee-controlled witch smiles and places a large hand gently upon your shoulder.&gt;

That's a fine poke in the eye for the Lich King, but I think we can do better.

Goregek take you to kill big mom of hardknuckles, eh? You lucky!

Dumb softknuckles squeal good!

&lt;Rakjak squeals loudly and breaks out laughing.&gt;

&lt;Orfus's whiskers bristle.&gt;

Pirates... Is there no end to the depths of their depravity?

We must recover the stolen artifacts and return them to this cursed place so that my people may once more know peace.

&lt;Zaela takes the gore-spattered length of chain and wraps it around her hand and wrist.&gt;

If the stories are true, &lt;name&gt;, it was on this length of chain that Deathwing had once fastened the Demon Soul, forged in his bid to control the other dragonflights. The Demon Stone has long been destroyed but perhaps this hunk of elementium holds some residual power...

You've done a great thing today.

ua:
&lt;Заела бере закривавлений шмат ланцюга й обмотує його навколо долоні та зап'ястка.&gt;

Якщо вірити переказам, &lt;name&gt;, саме до цього ланцюга Смертокрил колись прикріпив Демонічну душу, викувану, коли він прагнув підкорити інші драконячі стаї. Демонічний камінь давно знищено, але, можливо, у цьому шматку елементію ще лишилася залишкова сила...

Сьогодні тобі вдалося велике діло.

en:
Let's see what you've brought me...

&lt;He holds the phial up to the light and examines it closely.&gt;

Yes, this will do.  Well done, &lt;name&gt;.

&lt;Ulfang howls loudly at your defeat of his great eagle enemy.&gt;

The honor of the kill is yours. I wish that it had been my maw to finally close upon her neck.

Let us not waste the sacrifice that she has made for us. Here, eat them!

&lt;3 ... 2 ... 1 ...&gt;

&lt;You wet your fingers and snuff out the fuse. The cathedral is saved!&gt;

Underneath the powder kegs you find a heap of notes and papers. Apparently the cultists were trying to destroy the evidence behind them.&gt;

ua:
&lt;3... 2... 1...&gt;

&lt;Ти змочуєш пальці й гасиш ґніт. Собор врятовано!&gt;

Під бочками з порохом ти знаходиш купу нотаток і паперів. Вочевидь, сектанти намагалися знищити докази.

en:
This meat is disgusting! It's going to take every spice I have to cover that smell up.

Only the best for the Boss-Lady!

&lt;Sezik grins and winks at you.&gt;

ua:
Це м'ясо огидне! Піде вся моя приправа, щоб перебити цей сморід.

Для хазяйки — лише найкраще!

&lt;Сезік шкіриться й підморгує тобі.&gt;

en:
&lt;The deathguard rubs his hands together in anticipation.&gt;

Excellent. Their loss is my... our gain!

You didn't have trouble with any of these along the way? Some of them look rather unstable. I may be undead, but I value my existence!

&lt;You slap Bauden around until he wakes up.&gt;

&lt;class&gt;? What are you doing here?

I'm SI:7 Agent Jack Bauden. This is the longest day of my life.

ua:
&lt;Ти б'єш Бодена по щоках, поки він не прокидається.&gt;

{class}? Що ти тут робиш?

Я агент ШРУ Джек Боден. Це найдовший день у моєму житті.

en:
&lt;Mazoga gathers the pile of blood in his hands and raises it to his mouth. It liquifies and pours gorily down his throat.&gt;

Dey drink de blood, dey get de power. I drink dere blood...

&lt;Mazoga gives you a wide, blood-smeared grin.&gt;

&lt;Ameer deftly combines the keys and begins to read the markings on the newly formed key tablet.&gt;

"A thousand worlds shattered, a thousand worlds more to overcome... Such is the will of the Nexus-King."

&lt;Ameer turns the tablet over and begins to read from the back-side.&gt;

Stasis chambers of Bash'ir?

So Dokin drafted you to help with the candied sweet potatoes?

&lt;Francis smiles.&gt;

It's the only way he can keep up. Thanks for bringing these.

YES?! Do you see me interrupting your fascinating argument?

No... no, please, go ahead. I'm sure that your interruption is about something very important. More important than dealing with the survival of everyone here, in fact.

&lt;Fizzle taps his foot impatiently.&gt;

It's a chore keeping all these tables stocked. If you stop and think about it, it's strange going to so much trouble when we needn't eat anymore.

&lt;William shrugs.&gt;

Tradition is tradition.

Why have you come here, outsider?

&lt;You tell the elder that you were sent by Foriel Broadleaf at the Grove of the Ancients. He seems to relax slightly.&gt;

The elf is right. The forces of Felwood have seeped into Darkshore and sickened my people.

&lt;Seeing the map, Cinderfuse puts down her weapon.&gt;

I see ye found me map. Guess that means ye be a miner, too?

Well then, if yer lookin' fer booty, best bet would be ta check yer breeches. However, if ye lookin' fer work, then I got just the task fer ya.

I can feel it - like a dark shadow lifted from the land. Dead. My father is dead!

&lt;Wrathion takes the jaw fragment from you. His hands and face blur as he recites a dark enchantment, the gem clusters you collected earlier orbiting around his head. The jawpiece suddenly shatters, and with a terrible hissing sound your twin daggers awaken.&gt;

Your reward is ready. Take them, quickly. You will need them momentarily...

You are, indeed, a master of your craft. Nalice is dead, and it is time you are rewarded for your efforts.

&lt;Wrathion takes the vial from you, his face a mask of equal parts reverence and revulsion. He drops the gems you collected one-by-one into the blood, muttering an incantation.&gt;

&lt;Without warning he pours the blood over the blades of the daggers, and the steel seems to writhe and twist as though alive. When the smoke clears, the daggers have altered their shape.&gt;

&lt;Flintlocke greedily digs through the machine parts, tossing choice picks over his shoulder.&gt;

Oh aye, 'ere's the stuff.

&lt;He sticks his head all the way into one of the crates.&gt;

But where's me powder? Everything's here but for the powder. I need explosives, man!

You tell the King, no powder, no power. I need me some kersplosions or I ain't leavin' port.

ua:
&lt;Флінтлок жадібно порпається в деталях машини, кидаючи через плече обрані шматки.&gt;

О так, оце воно.

&lt;Він занурює голову аж у один з ящиків.&gt;

Але де ж мій порох? Тут усе є, окрім пороху. Мені потрібна вибухівка, чоловіче!

Передай королю: немає пороху — немає й ходу. Мені потрібні вибухи, бо інакше я з порту не зрушу.

en:
Er... what's this? A bear's head, by the looks of it.

&lt;He runs a finger along his scar unconsciously.&gt;

Well, that's quite an interesting kill you have yourself there. Couldn't be that bear from back then...

&lt;He trails off then starts to visibly shake.&gt;

Oh, take that away take it away! Get that grisly thing out of here!

ua:
Е-е... що це? Схоже, голова ведмедя.

&lt;Він несвідомо проводить пальцем по своєму шраму.&gt;

Що ж, доволі цікавий трофей у тебе тут. Невже той самий ведмідь із тих часів...

&lt;Він затихає, а тоді помітно починає тремтіти.&gt;

О, забери це, забери! Прибери цю жахливу штуку звідси!

en:
Mmm...

&lt;Senedras takes in the scent of the food you've brought him.&gt;

This smells delicious. Thank you, &lt;name&gt;.

ua:
Ммм...

&lt;Сенедрас вдихає запах їжі, яку ти йому приніс.&gt;

Пахне чудово. Дякую, &lt;name&gt;.

en:
&lt;Crusader Rhydalla's face pales as she reads the orders.&gt;

This can only mean one thing, &lt;name&gt;. The Black Knight is a member of the Cult of the Damned and has been sent by Arthas to disrupt the tournament!

The Black Knight has proven himself a fearsome combatant, and you will need to be every bit as good if you wish to face him. When you are a champion, return to me and we'll find a way to ensure his defeat.

&lt;Tiffany looks over the gem and nods her head.&gt;

Very good work, &lt;name&gt;. It seems your skills have improved since the last time you cut something for me.

Enjoy that design, it's one of my finest.

ua:
&lt;Тіффані оглядає самоцвіт і схвально киває.&gt;

Дуже гарна робота, {name}. Схоже, твоя майстерність покращилася відтоді, як ти востаннє $p(гранив:гранила) щось для мене.

Насолоджуйся цим ескізом, це один з моїх найкращих.

