en:
We saving pandaren, but the land still sad... Look, rain's not stopping at all!

&lt;Ken-Ken shakes his tiny fists at the sky.&gt;

How many more butts we gotta punch before we fix this town?!

&lt;The sky darkens in response.&gt;

You are very courageous to bring us this information. I was beginning to wonder why the blue dragonflight had so boldly initiated an attack upon the temple itself. Now we know that they are using enormous amounts of the very magic they view as such a threat to Azeroth.

&lt;The queen shakes her head in seeming resignation.&gt;

Hypocritical, but so be it. If Malygos will not come to his senses, we have no choice but to take action in response to their assault.

&lt;Pa'ku wipes a tear from her eye using her wing-claw.&gt;

That was a beautiful demonstration of commitment. Your hair looks lovely.

&lt;Pa'ku cackles.&gt;

&lt;Tolliver grasps the helmet reverently with quivering hands.&gt;

Rageroar's battleships intercepted our vessel as we fled from Gilneas. We were to be carried here as trophies to the Warchief. As we neared the shore, some of us fought back. Rageroar - he began killing indiscriminately - howling with laughter. Our ship capsized and he ordered his men to fire at us as we drowned. Few of us made it to land.

Afterwards, I learned that he wore my brother's scalp as... as a trophy.

&lt;He closes his eyes.&gt;

&lt;Halford reads the journal.&gt;

Abbendis has gone off the deep end. The Light speaks to her now?

Despite the inane ramblings, this journal gives us a never before seen look into the mind of the Scarlet zealots. This was a great find, &lt;name&gt;. Lord Fordragon will be pleased.

&lt;Stanwad takes the bundle from you and begins sorting the data.&gt;

Wow. How many people did you say died to get this information?

&lt;Stanwad shakes his head.&gt;

You'll be happy to know that what McSorf and his crew of bumbling imbeciles discovered is an ancient recipe for tundra stew. Did he not notice the icons of common vegetables and the pictograph of a humanoid mouth chompin' down on said veggies? You don't need a damned cipher to break this code!

&lt;Berrund the Gleaming appears not to have a speck of pollen on himself.&gt;

You got yourself good and covered in that lashroom dust, all right.

I'm a bit surprised you're not itching and sneezing, like your friend here.

I recognize those mandibles. Karanosh ate my brother, you know.

Of course, I have millions of brothers.

&lt;Zikk cackles.&gt;

What have you found, traveler? Ah, a scroll written in a mysterious language. Quite an interesting find!

&lt;Nola carefully examines the scroll.&gt;

I've never seen characters like these before, but perhaps Kugro has...

So you've brought Chellan's list. Excellent! I was hoping to receive this today. Let's see what she needs.

&lt;Nurguni reads over the list and begins placing various items in a box.&gt;

That's most of what she requested. The pieces for the beds are simply too large to be delivered by hippogryph, but I'll make arrangements to have them sent by wagon.

I send you to a Machine Speaker to get us into the speakeasy, and you wind up aiding the market reeve of the Forgegrounds in some roundabout delivery and trading operation?

&lt;Merrix smirks coyly as he claps his heavy stone hands in applause. It is a much quieter sound than you would imagine.&gt;

Well done, my resourceful outlander.

How kind of you to go into a secret facility, run by one of the most brilliant Keepers in existence, all to bring me back... this.

&lt;Theldren looks distastefully at the object, then starts to stare deeper.&gt;

Nevermind. I mean... I suppose I can make this work. Since you went to all the trouble of getting it for me.

&lt;You see him place the object close by him. His eyes dart to it occasionally while a mysterious smile plays over his lips&gt;

Meddlin' goblin bastards!

&lt;Moira takes a deep breath.&gt;

Sorry, I just canna abide those green miscreants any longer.

&lt;Mother Tauranook wipes her tears away.&gt;

There was once a time when I could walk across this tundra and the snow would fill my view for as far as I could see.

But the snow has left us - signaling that our time here has come to an end. We leave behind Taunka'le Village and the Borean Tundra with many happy memories...

&lt;Mother Tauranook whimpers.&gt;

Perhaps the future will welcome our return - along with the snow.

You were right to bring this to my attention. This could be a production order for additional fel reavers - or new attack plans! This will take some time to decipher. Leave me. I will summon you when I know more. 

&lt;Magister Bloodhawk nods to you as you turn to leave&gt; 

You are a sharp one, &lt;name&gt;. I shall be watching your progress with interest.

Nice shootin' out there!

And, hey, don't worry if you "accidentally" missed a Mechagnome or two... I did too!

&lt;Penny winks at you.&gt;

ua:
Гарна стрільба!

І, знаєш, не хвилюйся, якщо "випадково" промахну$p(вся:лася) повз пару механогномів... Я теж!

&lt;Пенні підморгує тобі.&gt;

en:
&lt;The Eye glimmers darkly, colors swirling about its dusky surface.&gt;

Ah, the succulent thrill of life extinguished. Do you feel it, &lt;class&gt;? Do you relish it as I do?

No, I see not. You fight to protect the lives of others. Pity.

&lt;Mallia removes her eyepatch and holds the black diamond before her empty eye socket.&gt;

What have we, what have we - breaches, the breaches number three. Two heads, one wholly given to its master. I see the future. A hammer united. A mountain shattered. Oh - OH!

&lt;Mallia drops the diamond to the floor, covering her face with her hands.&gt;

A-ha! Soul Remnants!

&lt;Khadgar cradles the Remnants briefly and focuses intently upon them.&gt;

There, now you and your companions may access the upper level of the Citadel directly.

She's alive?! That's great! I can't wait to catch up and see what she's been working on. I wasn't always a fan of Grizzek's -- he could really grind Saffy's gears! But if they're together again, then it's a packaged deal. Hmmmmm.

&lt;Kelsey looks thoughtful for a moment before a sly grin spreads across her face&gt;

I have an idea or two. You don't worry about a thing, &lt;name&gt;. Enjoy the parrot!

A few stubborn ranchers want to make my job harder?

&lt;The Watch Commander sighs.&gt;

Fine. I will rob no pandaren of his right to defend his land.

&lt;Duke Lankral nods his approval at your report of success.&gt;

We face a foe that dwarfs us, not only in stature, but also numerically. If we are to win the battle for Icecrown, we must outthink them!

With Ufrang dead, that gives us an advantage in Jotunheim. Let us see if we can capitalize on it.

The cliffwatcher was a Grimtotem spy?! No wonder we had no warning!

&lt;Thalia seethes with barely contained rage.&gt;

I don't want that damned thing. Throw it into the water and let the Longhorn name never be spoken again!

You... You're not Snivel. Did he send you? He's so late, I had started to give up hope...

&lt;Tears start welling up in the woman's eyes once she realizes that you aren't there to deliver a message from Snivel.&gt;

That's not like my Snivel, but what other choice is there?

&lt;Thagg listens intently as you recount your assault on Astranaar.&gt;

This is good news indeed, &lt;race&gt;. But right now, we need more than just good news here.

These triage kits will be put to good use!

Oh, so Takrin sent you?

&lt;Kargal warily eyes your recruitment letter and shoves it unceremoniously into his vest&gt;

I'll sign this when you've earned it. I've got reports from down south that this whole continent is being torn apart. Meanwhile, we've got supply caravans backed up to the river and outposts under siege from here to Stonetalon. You want to prove your worth to the horde? Start by proving it here.

&lt;Torcali's voice enters your mind.&gt;

Time and time again I have called upon you. Time and time again you have answered.

The little one tells me she will follow you wherever it is that you wish to go. After all that you have done for my faithful and my young, this is my gift to you.

From this day until the end of your days, you will wander not alone.

&lt;Torcali gently touches her great snout to your head.&gt;

Thank you and farewell, &lt;name&gt;.

ua:
&lt;У твоїй свідомості лунає голос Торкалі.&gt;

Знову й знову я кликала тебе. Знову й знову ти відповіда$p(в:ла).

Малеча каже, що піде за тобою, куди б ти не побажа$p(в:ла) вирушити. Після всього, що ти зроби$p(в:ла) для мого дитяти й моїх вірних, це буде моїм даром тобі.

Від сьогодні й до кінця твоїх днів ти не мандруватимеш наодинці.

&lt;Торкалі ніжно торкається твоєї голови своєю величезною мордою.&gt;

Дякую і прощавай, {name}.

en:
This power once belonged to my flight, passed down through my mother when she was empowered by the Titan, Eonar.

&lt;Merithra lowers her head for a moment.&gt;

If you are to use it to help save our world, then we must first bind these fragments together.

ua:
Ця сила колись належала моєму летові й дісталася від матері, коли її наділив могутністю титан Еонар.

&lt;Мерітра на мить опускає голову.&gt;

Якщо ти хочеш використати її, щоб урятувати наш світ, спершу ми маємо з'єднати ці уламки.

en:
Weapons, eh?

&lt;Force Commander Valen sighs.&gt;

I'm about to make an executive decision here, &lt;name&gt;. Let's hope this pays off, else King Wrynn will have my head!

Perfect.

&lt;Ang surveys the bruised turnips and the soggy watermelons.&gt;

What were they DOING down there!?

ua:
Чудово.

&lt;Анґ оглядає побиті ріпи та розмоклі кавуни.&gt;

Що вони там ВНИЗУ РОБИЛИ?!

en:
He will get up. Soon. Maybe not today, but soon.

And when he does...

&lt;A smile grows on Paosha's face.&gt;

Well these aren't as good as she deserves, but it will have to work.

&lt;Sully pats the dismantled ballista.&gt;

I'll get 'er up and runnin' in no time, just ye watch!

Collect ingredients and slay Cook Leathertongue in Atal'Utek.
