en:
&lt;Farseer Drek'Thar listens closely as you speak of your vision.&gt;

I see... these are truly dark days. Cho'gall has invaded the heart of Oshu'gun, draining the naaru of its life. He seeks to destroy the naaru, birthing a dark, void god in its place.

Cho'gall must be stopped. Come, we must travel to the sacred mountain before it is too late.

&lt;You hand the heart over to Alard. He places it within his forge and it begins to burn white hot.&gt;

Perhaps I should refer to you as Dragonslayer &lt;name&gt; from now on.

Joking aside, I'll begin my forging.

Was he able to translate it? 

&lt;You hand the book over to Seshuli and she begins to read it.&gt;

Dis is incredible. Dis earthen was able to create jewels with de light. And dose shrines he's built, I mean, he mentions building several of dem but...

&lt;Seshuli pulls out a few maps and begins scaninng them.&gt;

You imbued the burner with ley energy, eh? Let's have a look.

&lt;Deucus examines the leyflame burner.&gt;

Yes, this will do nicely! A crucial step in rebuilding the alchemy table.

A mana bomb?

&lt;Morran turns the fragment over in his hands.&gt;

It's nigh unthinkable! Even the best minds in Dalaran couldn't have conceived of a weapon like this. The sheer magnitude of the disturbance must've torn a rift in the nether, giving these creatures access to our lands.

We're here. Now, to cause a bit of trouble for the locals.

&lt;Nathanos looks at you, then at the rest of the group.&gt;

We don't look too conspicuous, do we?

How did you find me?

&lt;Anduin listens to you describe the vision from the Dream Brew.&gt;

Remarkable! That's exactly what happened several days ago. We've been laying low since then.

&lt;Leoroxx appraises you with a keen eye, seemingly trying to take your measure.&gt;

The death of Gnosh Brognat is a boon to all of the Mok'Nathal.  This is a good thing for you.

Let us see if we can push the boundaries of your prowess just a bit more.

Human children born of vrykul? And Ymiron ordered the deaths of all human born offspring?

&lt;Thoralius goes silent for a moment.&gt;

As much as I wish to deny what is so plainly presented to me, I cannot. There is no extinct "missing link" to humans as the Explorers' League proposed. The vrykul are the missing link. They are the progenitors of humanity.

&lt;Algerson examines the skull.&gt;

Now this... this is something! Why are my workers running, they should be harvesting!

We could make a killing with these!

Did you get stung by any bees? Did you feel the burn? Maybe you're allergic.

&lt;Faerin chuckles.&gt;

What? That wasn't a funny enough joke? Then you do better!

You're back! I was worried. Tell me everything.

&lt;Faerin looks you over.&gt; 

Those spiders didn't... do anything to you, did they? Didn't... plant eggs under your cloak or something? 

&lt;Faerin shivers.&gt;

A bit worse for the wear but still functional.

&lt;Thoralius reaches into the pouch and removes some odd looking roots.&gt;

Now to place them in the fire and inhale!

&lt;Thoralius throws the roots into the smoldering incense burner.&gt;

&lt;Thoralius inhales deeply. His body begins to quiver.&gt;

Wha... What... It cannot be... I cannot...

&lt;Your companion stares in awe.&gt;

No words to say... so beautiful! Can keep track of much more now. But what to count...

Aha! Count your things! No worry, am excellent counter. Woo-woo!

Huh? Well that sucks! Darn, I made thingsh worsh. In fact, I think I perfected their plague for them ...hic!

&lt;Peppy grimaces and takes a huge gulp of whatever noxious brew she's been drinking.&gt;

Well, I wash hoping that it wouldn't come down to thish, but it looks like there'sh no alternative ...hic.

&lt;Lessah examines the necklace.&gt;

How can this be?! All my research suggested that this belonged to Huln.

I'm sorry, &lt;name&gt;, but this necklace is a creation of the drogbar. I'll give it back to you to do with it what you want.

ua:
&lt;Лесса оглядає намисто.&gt;

Як таке може бути?! Усі мої дослідження вказували, що це належало Гулну.

Вибач, {name}, але це намисто — витвір дрогбарів. Я поверну його тобі, роби з ним, що хочеш.

en:
&lt;Lokra's gaze remains fixed on her dying frost wolf.&gt;

We had them... We had them, Asha. You were so fast. So beautiful.

I failed you, Asha. I am sorry.

&lt;Koltira takes the crystal shards from you and speaks in a quiet voice.&gt;

I remember these...

Lesser men would easily crumble beneath their assault. You have done well in removing their threat.

&lt;Tae'thelan takes the jewels from you and looks them over closely.&gt;

There may have been power in them once, but it's been all but drained. These are just pretty jewels now.

Here, take them. Consider them payment for your services here.

ua:
&lt;Тей'телан бере в тебе самоцвіти й уважно їх оглядає.&gt;

Можливо, колись у них і була сила, але тепер вона майже повністю вичерпана. Тепер це просто гарні камені.

Ось, візьми їх. Вважай це платою за твою службу тут.

en:
You save the wolves! So brave! Someday, maybe you get a wolf just like that to ride.

&lt;Dorak looks at the burning stables, then at the nearby river.&gt;

What should I do now?

Is that mana wine? For me?

&lt;Iadreth hungrily gulps down the bottle.&gt;

You and this Astoril have my thanks. I would surely have perished out here.

ua:
Це манавино? Для мене?

&lt;Іадрет жадібно вихиляє пляшку.&gt;

Дякую тобі й цьому Асторілу. Я б точно тут загинула.

en:
Let us observe a minute of silence for our fallen mates, &lt;name&gt;.

&lt;The Bloodsail Traitor grins at you and winks.&gt;

Being a traitor is one thing, murdering yer own buckos... that'd be just downright despicable, aye!

ua:
Вшануймо хвилиною мовчання наших полеглих товаришів, &lt;name&gt;.

&lt;Зрадник із Кривавого Вітрила посміхається тобі й підморгує.&gt;

Бути зрадником — це одне, а вбивати власних хлопців... це вже просто підло, ага!

en:
Hey, thanks, kid. Give it over, let's take a look.

&lt;He takes the device from you and fiddles with it.&gt;

Oh, that ain't good.

&lt;Salazae looks distraught.&gt;

Oh! Valjabu... why did you go on without me?

&lt;A ghostly tear drops from her eye.&gt;

Thank you, stranger. Now I can pass on with no regrets.

ua:
&lt;Салазе виглядає засмученою.&gt;

Ох! Валджабу... чому ти пішов без мене?

&lt;Примарна сльоза скочується з її ока.&gt;

Дякую тобі, $p(незнайомцю:незнайомко). Тепер я можу піти, ні про що не шкодуючи.

en:
&lt;Altruis nods knowingly.&gt;

I saw it too.

We must consider our next move carefully.

ua:
&lt;Алтруїс розуміюче киває.&gt;

Я теж це бачив.

Нам треба ретельно обміркувати наступний крок.

en:
&lt;Tor'chunk grins at the story that you tell him about your adventures at Boulder'mok.&gt;

Ah, I wish that I could have been there with you.  Let me tell you something, &lt;name&gt;: never accept any duty that keeps you from the glory of battle!

Hah!  After all of the ogre killing that you've done, are there any still left in these mountains for me?!

&lt;Dealer Hazzin lowers his voice to a whisper.&gt;

Ah, I know of your mission.  It is one of great importance to Nexus-Prince Haramad!

Now that we know the location of this first triangulation point, you must move swiftly to find the second!

&lt;Thassarian takes the crystal shards from you and speaks in a quiet voice.&gt;

I remember these...

Lesser men would easily crumble beneath their assault. You have done well in removing their threat.

You have done it!

&lt;Goraluk takes the items from your hands, and turns his back for a few moments&gt;

Now, I will touch this Sigil to your hand, and the entrance to the Crucible will open at your touch. Good luck.

Collect a Cask of Vintner's Golden.
Vintner's Golden (1)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(249732, 0, 1, null, null));

ua:
Збери бочку золотистого вина винороба.
Золотисте вино винороба (1)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(249732, 0, 1, null, null));

en:
&lt;Khadgar's face is ashen.&gt;

Draenor is saved, &lt;name&gt;. But the Legion is more powerful than even I had imagined. And Gul'dan, that snake - he's still alive. Somewhere.

Stay here and celebrate with the others, &lt;name&gt;. You've earned it. But I will soon return to Azeroth to deal with this, and I hope you will join me there when the time comes.

&lt;The sage grunts his approval at your actions on his behalf.&gt;

Perhaps I will be able to find the time soon to study these artifacts and come to an understanding of their significance.

But now there are more pressing matters to attend to.

&lt;Thiah Redmane's eyes widen as you describe the results of the experiment.&gt;

But, how could that happen? I'm certain I prepared the antidote correctly!

I've seen it work with spider and snake venoms, so why would it backfire here? Perhaps that's one of Outland's many peculiarities, &lt;name&gt;. I'd best pass this information along to my comrades.

Yes!  You've saved more spore sacs.

You're different than the other outsiders.  I'll let my people know about your deeds!

&lt;This quest is repeatable up to friendly reputation.&gt;

Great, I'll get up there and... harvest them soon.

&lt;Cousin Gootfur begins wrapping long strips of linen around his hands.&gt;

Can't believe I thought this was a good idea.

Collect blood from the beasts north of the Night Trench.
16Predator Blood (16)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(243350, 0, 16, null, null));

ua:
Збери кров звірів на північ від Нічного рову.
16Кров хижака (16)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(243350, 0, 16, null, null));

en:
Collect a Weathered Shrine Piece.
Weathered Shrine Piece (1)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(239494, 0, 1, null, null));

ua:
Збери Вивітрений уламок святилища.
Вивітрений уламок святилища (1)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(239494, 0, 1, null, null));

en:
It's locked, isn't it?  It looks pretty ordinary.

&lt;Lieutenant Dumont Shakes the chest, producing a rattling wooden sound.&gt;

No matter, I suppose.  If this gets us the edge we need against the Horde, then I could care less if the cure for the Plague was in there.

&lt;The greatmother nods her approval of your actions.&gt;

Thank you, &lt;name&gt;, you have done what is right and you have bought us a little more time to finish our preparations for leaving. We will soon make the journey north.

I am too old; when we go, I will not be able to carry everything with me. Would you like to take one of these?

&lt;Myralion takes the hilt from you and scrutinizes the artifact.&gt;

This came from the citadel? What was it doing there? This blade is certainly not of Scourge manufacture.

Weapons of this quality can only be crafted by a few of Azeroth's creatures. We will have to consult them and see if they can help us identify it.

&lt;Bloodhilt looks at the badges, then allows them to spill from his hands onto the sands below. His lips curl open into a toothy grin.&gt;

Now THIS is what I like to see, &lt;class&gt;! What is your name again?

You will go far here.

&lt;Highlord Mograine eyes you in silence for a moment.&gt;

You seem to have endured this leg of your trial admirably, &lt;race&gt;.

Pray that fate continues to smile upon you in your endeavor...

ua:
&lt;Верховний лорд Могрейн мовчки дивиться на тебе.&gt;

Ти гідно впора$p(вся:лася) з цим етапом випробування, &lt;раса&gt;.

Молися, щоб доля й надалі усміхалася тобі в твоєму починанні...

en:
&lt;You explain what happened in Stormwind.&gt;

Typical humans. Extorting allies because only their suffering matters.

&lt;Daniss takes a deep breath to steady herself.&gt;

I am sorry, &lt;name&gt;. I spoke out of frustration.

I'm no stranger to war, but Sylvanas' tactics have made this one exceptionally taxing. I didn't mean to discourage their... resourcefulness. I simply wish it hadn't come to it.

At this time, we must keep our faith in the Alliance.

ua:
&lt;Ти розповідаєш про те, що сталося у Штормовії.&gt;

Типові люди. Вимагають в союзників, наче важливі лише їхні страждання.

&lt;Данісс робить глибокий вдих, щоб опанувати себе.&gt;

Вибач, {name}. Я сказала це через розчарування.

Війна для мене не новина, але тактика Сильвани робить цю війну особливо виснажливою. Я не хотіла применшувати їхню... винахідливість. Просто шкода, що до цього дійшло.

Зараз нам треба зберігати віру в Альянс.

en:
&lt;Kirge listens intently and then falls to one knee.&gt;

Alive! My boy still lives! Praise to the earthmother, I still have a son.

&lt;Kirge composes himself.&gt;

&lt;class&gt;, my boy's mother didn't make it out of Taurajo alive. I will avenge her death, even if it means my son grows up without either of his parents.

ua:
&lt;Кірґе уважно слухає, а тоді опускається на одне коліно.&gt;

Живий! Мій хлопчик живий! Хвала Матері-Землі, в мене ще є син.

&lt;Кірґе опановує себе.&gt;

&lt;клас&gt;, мати мого хлопчика не вибралася з Таурайо живою. Я помщуся за її смерть, навіть якщо мій син зростатиме без обох батьків.

en:
You there! What is this nonsense falling into my domain? Green fire raining from the Maelstrom! Are you surface dwellers behind this?

&lt;You explain everything to the Stonemother.&gt;

A missing artifact, hm? I have not seen it, but I know where to start. You help the Stonemother, yes, and she will help you.

ua:
Гей, ти! Що за нісенітниця падає в мої володіння? Зелений вогонь ллється дощем із Мальстрему! Це ви, поверхневі мешканці, у цьому винні?

&lt;Ти пояснюєш усе Матері-Скелі.&gt;

Зниклий артефакт, кажеш? Я його не бачила, але знаю, звідки почати пошуки. Ти допоможеш Матері-Скелі — і вона допоможе тобі.

en:
&lt;Leoric takes the cards from you.&gt;

I will get these to our recorder and deliver the grim news to the families of the miners.

There is still much to be done if we are to succeed here and ultimately at the Wrathgate. Lord Fordragon is depending on us.

Hey, thanks, kid. Give it over, let's take a look.

&lt;He takes the device from you and fiddles with it.&gt;

Oh, that ain't good.

&lt;Jay listens to your account of the day's events.&gt;

I see. We'll keep an eye on the Ungas from here. And we'll do our best not to fish these waters too heavily, either. No doubt we're part of the problem, too.

Until next time, &lt;name&gt;.

&lt;The sapper grumbles as if he wishes that you hadn't succeeded.&gt;

The captain will be pleased to hear of your success.

You know, since you've been such a good sport in dealing with this Whisper Gulch business, why don't you take your pick of one of these?

My sister's vision must not come to pass!

&lt;Alleria seems frustrated.&gt;

I wish I could return, but that's simply not possible. There are things I can do here, however, and you two can help while we discuss the matter.

&lt;The Archmage looks damp and uncomfortable.&gt;

I apologize for the conditions here, &lt;name&gt;. I had no choice. I summoned this tower at the optimal confluence of arcane energies. My hope is to finish my work here before all my books get musty.

So then! Let's get to it.

Aha, I admit I hadn't expected to receive this.

&lt;The Weaver runs her pedipalps over the secret-woven silk, delighted.&gt;

Very interesting. I will have to keep this in mind.

&lt;Alaria quickly eats the meat that you cooked.&gt;

By the Light... I feel so much better.

You need to keep moving... quilboar have kidnapped the expedition, including Captain Garrick's son!

ua:
&lt;Аларія швидко з'їдає м'ясо, яке ти приготува$p(в:ла).&gt;

Світлом клянусь... мені набагато краще.

Тобі треба рухатися далі... свинобрази викрали експедицію, включно із сином Капітана Ґерріка!

en:
Bring the Lynx Paw to Er'inye.
Corroded Key (1)
Mummified Lynx's Paw (1)



